text: >-
  Yet another issue regards how the FBI knew to speak to Lance, and when they
  knew. Tyler does

  not seem to have been cooperative, and so the only official answer to this
  question seems to be

  that a member of the Robinson family told them about Lance. Yet it seems that
  by sending

  Agent Lance South the FBI were well prepared. Even if one accepts the
  untenable position that

  the SBI only met up with Tyler after 11:30 pm (having gotten word only around
  8 pm of Mike

  Mitchell's tip), it remains that agents could not have been sent at that time
  if they were to reach

  Lance (presumably driving to his home and taking him to the sheriff's office
  in Hurricane, a 40

  minute round trip), the latest they could have set out being around 8:50 pm.
  The only official

  response as far as we can see is that the South-bound posse just happened to
  be very well

  resourced with both SBI and FBI agents makina the lond iournev to the border
  reaion.
